<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neva River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Neva</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Neva is a short but powerful river of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, flowing about 74 kilometres from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ladoga">Lake Ladoga</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-finland">Gulf of Finland</a>. It formed a key route between the Baltic and Novgorod and was long contested between Novgorod, later Russia, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-nevsky">Alexander Nevsky</a> won his name defeating the Swedes on it in 1240. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-petersburg">Saint Petersburg</a> at its mouth in 1703.</p></div>
